    \begin{pmatrix}
        \cos({\pi}/{2}) & -\sin({\pi}/{2}) \\
        \sin({\pi}/{2}) & \cos({\pi}/{2})
    \end{pmatrix}
    = \begin{pmatrix}
        0 & -1 \\
        1 & 0
    \end{pmatrix}.

Applying the transformation to \mathbf{u} = (2, 1):Rot\left( \frac{\pi}{2} \right) \cdot \mathbf{u} =
    \begin{pmatrix}
        0 & -1 \\
        1 & 0
    \end{pmatrix}
    \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}
